IMPORT prelude

-- Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (Western Australia) -- the three instruments a person makes for their own future
-- incapacity: the enduring power of attorney (Part 9: ss 104, 104B, 104C, 105, 106, 107), the enduring power of guardianship
-- (Part 9A: ss 110B-110G) and the advance health directive (Part 9B: ss 110P-110T), with the order of priority for treatment
-- decisions (s 110ZJ) and for other personal matters (s 119), and the plenary guardian's functions and limits in s 45 that
-- s 110G(1) gives an enduring guardian.
--
-- Edition: compilation from legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc 49107, retrieved 7 September 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49107.txt. The deposit names no compilation number; its compilation table ends with the
-- Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Amendment (Sex or Gender Changes) Act 2024 Pt 4 Div 9 (in force 30 May 2025), the last
-- reprint listed is Reprint 5 as at 5 March 2010, and the uncommenced provisions table lists the Acts Amendment (Consent to Medical
-- Treatment) Act 2008 s 11 (so far as it inserts ss 110RA, 110ZAA-110ZAC) and s 12, and the Assisted Reproductive Technology and
-- Surrogacy Act 2025 Pt 17 Div 10 (not shown).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement au/wa:REQ-0006 (priority 1), raised 8 times by the three Western Australian cradle-to-grave lives
-- (Chloe c025, c082, c091, c095; Jake k092, k096; Daniel d085, d090). The lives ask: what may Chloe do at 18 (an enduring power of
-- attorney); who may be an attorney; what may an enduring guardian decide; who may make an advance health directive and when does it
-- operate; and, for Jake after his stroke, who decides for him if he cannot. SCOPED to Parts 9, 9A and 9B as those questions need
-- them, with the definitions (s 3, s 102), conditions and exceptions needed to answer them.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: Parts 1-8 (the Tribunal, guardianship and administration orders, the Public Advocate) except the s 45 list that
-- s 110G borrows; s 104A, s 110O and s 110ZA (recognition of interstate and foreign instruments), save that s 107(2) appears as one flag; s 108 (effect of an
-- administration order on an enduring power of attorney); s 109 (Tribunal intervention) except as the route by which a donee may be
-- released; ss 110H, 110J-110N, 110V-110Z (Tribunal declarations and directions); Part 9C (who is the person responsible, s 110ZD);
-- Part 9D Subdivisions 1 and 3 (urgent treatment; abortion) and s 110ZIB; Part 9E (medical research). The forms for an enduring
-- power of guardianship and an advance health directive are "prescribed by the regulations"; the regulations were not retrieved,
-- so whether the form was followed is an INPUT. Whether a person has "full legal capacity" or is "unable to make reasonable
-- judgments" is a finding of fact the Act does not define; both are INPUTS.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) -- enduring powers and advance health directives`

§§ `helpers`

-- Dates are given as year, month and day; the age is in completed years on the given day.
GIVEN `birth year` IS A NUMBER, `birth month` IS A NUMBER, `birth day` IS A NUMBER, `on year` IS A NUMBER, `on month` IS A NUMBER, `on day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`age in completed years` MEANS
    IF `on month` GREATER THAN `birth month` OR (`on month` EQUALS `birth month` AND `on day` AT LEAST `birth day`)
    THEN `on year` MINUS `birth year`
    ELSE `on year` MINUS `birth year` MINUS 1

-- The same two-witness rule appears three times, in s 104(2)(a), s 110E(1)(c) and (f), and s 110Q(1)(d): "2 persons -- (i) both of
-- whom are authorised by law to take declarations; or (ii) of whom -- (I) one is authorised by law to take declarations; and (II) the
-- other has the qualifications specified in subsection ...". The qualifications differ by instrument (see each section below); the
-- caller counts only witnesses who have them.
GIVEN `witnesses authorised to take declarations` IS A NUMBER, `other qualified witnesses` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the two-witness rule is met` IF
        `witnesses authorised to take declarations` AT LEAST 2
    OR  (`witnesses authorised to take declarations` AT LEAST 1 AND `other qualified witnesses` AT LEAST 1)

§§ `104(1a), 110B, 110P -- who may make each instrument`

-- s 104(1a): "A person who has reached 18 years of age and has full legal capacity may create an enduring power of attorney."
-- s 110B: "A person who has reached 18 years of age and has full legal capacity may make an enduring power of guardianship ..."
-- s 110P: "A person who has reached 18 years of age and has full legal capacity may make an advance health directive containing
-- treatment decisions in respect of the person's future treatment."
-- The test is the same for all three. "Full legal capacity" is not defined in s 3; it is an input.
DECLARE Instrument IS ONE OF
    `an enduring power of attorney`
    `an enduring power of guardianship`
    `an advance health directive`

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument, `age of the maker` IS A NUMBER, `the maker has full legal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may make the instrument` IF
        `age of the maker` AT LEAST 18
    AND `the maker has full legal capacity`

§§ `104C, 110D -- who may be appointed`

-- s 104C: "A person is eligible to be appointed as a donee or substitute donee of an enduring power of attorney if the person has
-- reached 18 years of age and has full legal capacity."
-- s 110D: "A person is eligible to be appointed under section 110B or 110C(1) if the person has reached 18 years of age and has full
-- legal capacity."
-- Part 9B appoints no-one: an advance health directive contains the maker's own treatment decisions (s 110P).
-- Nothing in ss 104C or 110D excludes a relative, a spouse, or a person who will inherit.
GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument, `age of the appointee` IS A NUMBER, `the appointee has full legal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is eligible to be appointed under the instrument` IF
    CONSIDER `the instrument`
    WHEN `an advance health directive` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `age of the appointee` AT LEAST 18 AND `the appointee has full legal capacity`

§§ `104 -- creating an enduring power of attorney`

-- s 104(1): created "by instrument -- (a) that is in the form or substantially in the form of Form 1 in Schedule 3; and (b) in which
-- the donor of the power declares that the power either -- (i) will continue in force notwithstanding his subsequent legal
-- incapacity; or (ii) will be in force only during any period when a declaration by the State Administrative Tribunal under section
-- 106 that the donor does not have legal capacity is in force."
-- s 104(2): "not effective ... unless -- (a) there are 2 attesting witnesses ... and (b) the instrument has endorsed on it, or annexed
-- to it, a statement of acceptance in the form, or substantially in the form, of Form 2 in Schedule 3 executed by -- (i) the person or
-- persons appointed to be the donee of the power; and (ii) where applicable, the person or persons appointed to be the substitute
-- donee of the power."
-- s 104(3): the second kind of witness "must be a person -- (a) who has reached 18 years of age; and (b) who is not a person appointed
-- to be a donee or substitute donee of the power."
-- Schedule 3 is not in the deposit (only its heading), so following Form 1 and Form 2 is an input. Unlike s 110E and s 110Q,
-- s 104 says nothing about who signs or about the witnesses signing in each other's presence.
DECLARE AttorneyInstrument HAS
    `in the form or substantially in the form of Form 1` IS A BOOLEAN
    `declares it continues despite later incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `declares it is in force only while a section 106 declaration is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `attesting witnesses authorised to take declarations` IS A NUMBER
    `other attesting witnesses aged 18 or more who are not a donee or substitute donee` IS A NUMBER
    `statement of acceptance executed by every donee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a substitute donee is appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statement of acceptance executed by every substitute donee` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the power` IS AN AttorneyInstrument, `age of the donor` IS A NUMBER, `the donor has full legal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an enduring power of attorney is created` IF
        `the person may make the instrument` `an enduring power of attorney` `age of the donor` `the donor has full legal capacity`
    AND `the power`'s `in the form or substantially in the form of Form 1`
    AND (    `the power`'s `declares it continues despite later incapacity`
         OR  `the power`'s `declares it is in force only while a section 106 declaration is in force`)
    AND `the two-witness rule is met` (`the power`'s `attesting witnesses authorised to take declarations`) (`the power`'s `other attesting witnesses aged 18 or more who are not a donee or substitute donee`)
    AND `the power`'s `statement of acceptance executed by every donee`
    AND (    (NOT `the power`'s `a substitute donee is appointed`)
         OR  `the power`'s `statement of acceptance executed by every substitute donee`)

§§ `104(1)(b), 105, 106 -- when an enduring power of attorney is in force`

-- s 105(1): "an enduring power of attorney that is in force is not affected by the subsequent legal incapacity of the donor".
-- s 105(2): an act of the donee "during a period of legal incapacity of the donor is as effective as if the donor were of full legal
-- capacity."
-- s 106(2): the Tribunal may declare "that the donor does not have legal capacity and that the power of attorney is in force" if the
-- person "(a) is the donor of an enduring power of attorney referred to in section 104(1)(b)(ii); and (b) is unable, by reason of a
-- mental disability, to make reasonable judgments in respect of matters relating to all or any part of his estate".
-- s 3: "mental disability includes an intellectual disability, a psychiatric condition, an acquired brain injury and dementia".
-- INFERENCE: a power of the s 104(1)(b)(i) kind is in force from its creation, while the donor still has capacity -- the declaration
-- is that it "will continue in force", which presupposes it is already in force. The Act does not say so in terms.
DECLARE AttorneyKind IS ONE OF
    `a continuing power`
    `a power that springs on a section 106 declaration`

GIVEN `the kind` IS AN AttorneyKind, `the donor has a mental disability` IS A BOOLEAN, `the donor is unable to make reasonable judgments about the estate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Tribunal may declare the donor lacks legal capacity` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a power that springs on a section 106 declaration` THEN `the donor has a mental disability` AND `the donor is unable to make reasonable judgments about the estate`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the kind` IS AN AttorneyKind, `a section 106 declaration is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the enduring power of attorney is in force` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a continuing power` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `a section 106 declaration is in force`

§§ `107 -- obligations of the donee`

-- s 107(1): the donee "(a) shall exercise his powers as attorney with reasonable diligence to protect the interests of the donor ...;
-- (b) shall keep and preserve accurate records and accounts of all dealings and transactions made under the power; (c) subject to
-- section 109(2), may not renounce a power during any period of legal incapacity of the donor; and (d) shall, if the donee becomes
-- bankrupt, report that bankruptcy to the State Administrative Tribunal. Penalty applicable to paragraph (b): $2 000."
-- s 107(2): for a power recognised under s 104A(2), "subsection (1)(c) does not apply".
-- s 109(2)(a): the donee may apply for an order "revoking or varying the terms of an enduring power of attorney, appointing a
-- substitute donee ...". INFERENCE: such an order is the "subject to section 109(2)" release; and the Act does not stop a donee
-- renouncing while the donor has capacity.
`section 107(1)(b) maximum penalty` MEANS 2000

GIVEN `the donor is legally incapable` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Tribunal has made a section 109 order on the donee's application` IS A BOOLEAN, `the power is recognised under section 104A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the donee may renounce` IF
        (NOT `the donor is legally incapable`)
    OR  `the Tribunal has made a section 109 order on the donee's application`
    OR  `the power is recognised under section 104A`

§§ `110E -- formal requirements for an enduring power of guardianship`

-- s 110E(1): "not valid unless -- (a) it is in the form or substantially in the form prescribed by the regulations; and (b) it is
-- signed by the appointor or by another person in the presence of, and at the direction of, the appointor; and (c) the signature ...
-- is witnessed by 2 persons ...; and (d) it is signed by the witnesses ... in the presence of -- (i) the appointor; and (ii) the
-- person who signed it at the appointor's direction (if applicable); and (iii) each other; and (e) it is signed by each person being
-- appointed as an enduring guardian or substitute enduring guardian (an appointee) to indicate the appointee's acceptance of the
-- appointment; and (f) the signature of the appointee is witnessed by 2 persons ...; and (g) it is signed by the witnesses referred to
-- in paragraph (f) in the presence of the appointee and each other."
-- s 110E(2): the second kind of witness must have "reached 18 years of age" and not be "(i) the appointor; or (ii) the person who
-- signed the enduring power of guardianship at the appointor's direction (if applicable); or (iii) an appointee."
-- The form is prescribed by regulations that were not retrieved: an input.
DECLARE GuardianshipInstrument HAS
    `in the prescribed form or substantially so` IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed by the appointor, or for them in their presence and at their direction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appointor's signature -- witnesses authorised to take declarations` IS A NUMBER
    `appointor's signature -- other adult witnesses who are not the appointor, the signer or an appointee` IS A NUMBER
    `those witnesses signed in the presence of the appointor, any signer and each other` IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed by every appointee to accept` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appointee's signature -- witnesses authorised to take declarations` IS A NUMBER
    `appointee's signature -- other adult witnesses who are not the appointor, the signer or an appointee` IS A NUMBER
    `those witnesses signed in the presence of the appointee and each other` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the power` IS A GuardianshipInstrument, `age of the appointor` IS A NUMBER, `the appointor has full legal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an enduring power of guardianship is valid` IF
        `the person may make the instrument` `an enduring power of guardianship` `age of the appointor` `the appointor has full legal capacity`
    AND `the power`'s `in the prescribed form or substantially so`
    AND `the power`'s `signed by the appointor, or for them in their presence and at their direction`
    AND `the two-witness rule is met` (`the power`'s `appointor's signature -- witnesses authorised to take declarations`) (`the power`'s `appointor's signature -- other adult witnesses who are not the appointor, the signer or an appointee`)
    AND `the power`'s `those witnesses signed in the presence of the appointor, any signer and each other`
    AND `the power`'s `signed by every appointee to accept`
    AND `the two-witness rule is met` (`the power`'s `appointee's signature -- witnesses authorised to take declarations`) (`the power`'s `appointee's signature -- other adult witnesses who are not the appointor, the signer or an appointee`)
    AND `the power`'s `those witnesses signed in the presence of the appointee and each other`

§§ `110F, 110G, 45 -- when an enduring guardian may act, and what they may decide`

-- s 110F: "An enduring power of guardianship has effect, subject to its terms, at any time the appointor is unable to make reasonable
-- judgments in respect of matters relating to his or her person."
-- s 110G(1): an enduring guardian "has the same functions under section 45(1) and (2), and is subject to the same limitations under
-- sections 45(3), (3A), (4A) and (4), 110ZR and 110ZT, in relation to the appointor as a plenary guardian has". (2) the power "may
-- limit the functions ... to the functions specified in the power"; (3) may limit "the circumstances in which the enduring guardian
-- may act".
-- s 45(1): the functions "in respect of the person" of a parent with parental responsibility, "as if the represented person were a
-- child lacking in mature understanding, but a plenary guardian does not ... have the right to chastise or punish".
-- s 45(2): "(a) decide where the represented person is to live ...; (b) decide with whom the represented person is to live; (c) decide
-- whether the represented person should work ...; (d) subject to subsections (3A) and (4A), make treatment decisions ...; (e) decide
-- what education and training the represented person is to receive; (f) decide with whom the represented person is to associate;
-- (g) ... commence, conduct or settle any legal proceedings on behalf of the represented person, except proceedings relating to the
-- estate of the represented person".
-- s 45(3): "cannot ... (a) vote in any election; ... (c) consent ... to the adoption of a child ...; (d) under the Marriage Act 1961
-- ... give consent in relation to the marriage of a minor, sign a notice of intended marriage or take part in the solemnization of a
-- marriage". (3A): "cannot make a decision in respect of the performance of an abortion". (4A)(b): "cannot consent to the
-- sterilisation ... except in accordance with Division 3" (not encoded). (4): "may not make a will or other testamentary disposition".
-- INFERENCE: selling the appointor's property is a matter of the estate, not "the person": it falls to an attorney (Part 9) or an
-- administrator, not to an enduring guardian.
DECLARE PersonalDecision IS ONE OF
    `where the appointor lives`
    `with whom the appointor lives`
    `whether and where the appointor works`
    `a treatment decision other than an abortion`
    `what education and training the appointor receives`
    `with whom the appointor associates`
    `bringing legal proceedings for the appointor not about the estate`
    `bringing legal proceedings about the appointor's estate`
    `voting for the appointor in an election`
    `consenting to an adoption`
    `signing a notice of intended marriage for the appointor`
    `consenting to an abortion`
    `making a will for the appointor`
    `selling the appointor's house`
    `punishing the appointor`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A PersonalDecision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 45 gives a plenary guardian the decision` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `where the appointor lives` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `with whom the appointor lives` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `whether and where the appointor works` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a treatment decision other than an abortion` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `what education and training the appointor receives` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `with whom the appointor associates` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `bringing legal proceedings for the appointor not about the estate` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the decision` IS A PersonalDecision, `the appointor is unable to make reasonable judgments about their person` IS A BOOLEAN, `the power limits the function or circumstances to exclude it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the enduring guardian may make the decision` IF
        `the appointor is unable to make reasonable judgments about their person`
    AND `section 45 gives a plenary guardian the decision` `the decision`
    AND (NOT `the power limits the function or circumstances to exclude it`)

§§ `110Q, 110R -- making a valid advance health directive`

-- s 110Q(1): "not valid unless -- (a) it is in the form or substantially in the form prescribed by the regulations; and (b) the maker
-- is encouraged to seek legal or medical advice; and (c) it is signed by its maker or by another person in the presence of, and at the
-- direction of, its maker; and (d) the signature ... is witnessed by 2 persons ...; and (e) it is signed by the witnesses in the
-- presence of -- (i) its maker; and (ii) the person who signed it at its maker's direction (if applicable); and (iii) each other."
-- s 110Q(2): "Despite subsection (1)(b), the validity of an advance health directive is not affected by a failure to comply with
-- subsection (1)(b)."
-- s 110Q(3): the second kind of witness must have "reached 18 years of age" and not be "(i) the maker ...; or (ii) the person who
-- signed the directive at its maker's direction". A relative, a beneficiary or a treating doctor is not excluded.
-- s 110R: a treatment decision "is invalid if [it] -- (a) is not made voluntarily; or (b) is made as a result of inducement or
-- coercion", or if "at the time the directive is made, its maker does not understand -- (a) the nature of the treatment decision; or
-- (b) the consequences of making the treatment decision."
DECLARE Directive HAS
    `in the prescribed form or substantially so` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the maker was encouraged to seek legal or medical advice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed by the maker, or for them in their presence and at their direction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `witnesses authorised to take declarations` IS A NUMBER
    `other adult witnesses who are not the maker or the signer` IS A NUMBER
    `the witnesses signed in the presence of the maker, any signer and each other` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the directive` IS A Directive, `age of the maker` IS A NUMBER, `the maker has full legal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the advance health directive is valid` IF
        `the person may make the instrument` `an advance health directive` `age of the maker` `the maker has full legal capacity`
    AND `the directive`'s `in the prescribed form or substantially so`
    AND `the directive`'s `signed by the maker, or for them in their presence and at their direction`
    AND `the two-witness rule is met` (`the directive`'s `witnesses authorised to take declarations`) (`the directive`'s `other adult witnesses who are not the maker or the signer`)
    AND `the directive`'s `the witnesses signed in the presence of the maker, any signer and each other`

GIVEN `made voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN, `made as a result of inducement or coercion` IS A BOOLEAN, `the maker understood its nature and consequences when made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the treatment decision is valid under section 110R` IF
        `made voluntarily`
    AND (NOT `made as a result of inducement or coercion`)
    AND `the maker understood its nature and consequences when made`

§§ `110S, 110T -- when a treatment decision in a directive operates`

-- s 110S(1): it operates "(a) at any time the maker of the directive is unable to make reasonable judgments in respect of that
-- treatment; and (b) as if -- (i) the treatment decision had been made by the maker at that time; and (ii) the maker were of full
-- legal capacity." (2): "operates only in the circumstances specified in the directive." (3): it "does not operate if circumstances
-- exist or have arisen that -- (a) the maker of that directive would not have reasonably anticipated at the time of making the
-- directive; and (b) would have caused a reasonable person in the maker's position to have changed his or her mind".
-- s 110S(4): matters to be taken into account under (3) include "the maker's age at the time the directive was made and at the time
-- the treatment decision would otherwise operate" and "the period that has elapsed between those times" -- weighed, not encoded.
-- s 110S(6): "Subject to section 110T, a treatment decision ... is taken to have been revoked if the maker of the directive has changed
-- his or her mind about the treatment decision since making the directive."
-- s 110T: not revoked, and no change of mind, "merely because the maker subsequently makes an enduring power of guardianship (whether
-- about the same matter as the treatment decision or a different matter)."
GIVEN `the maker has changed their mind since making it` IS A BOOLEAN, `the only sign of that is a later enduring power of guardianship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the treatment decision is taken to be revoked` IF
        `the maker has changed their mind since making it`
    AND (NOT `the only sign of that is a later enduring power of guardianship`)

GIVEN `the maker is unable to make reasonable judgments about the treatment` IS A BOOLEAN, `within the circumstances the directive specifies` IS A BOOLEAN, `unanticipated circumstances would change a reasonable person's mind` IS A BOOLEAN, `the decision is revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the treatment decision operates` IF
        `the maker is unable to make reasonable judgments about the treatment`
    AND `within the circumstances the directive specifies`
    AND (NOT `unanticipated circumstances would change a reasonable person's mind`)
    AND (NOT `the decision is revoked`)

§§ `110ZJ, 119 -- who decides, in order`

-- s 110ZJ(1): applies "if a patient is unable to make reasonable judgments in respect of any treatment proposed" (subject to the urgent
-- treatment Subdivision and s 110ZIB, not encoded). (2): "If the patient has made an advance health directive containing a treatment
-- decision in respect of the treatment, whether or not the treatment is provided ... must be decided in accordance with the treatment
-- decision." (3): if not, an enduring guardian who "(i) is authorised to make a treatment decision in respect of the treatment; and
-- (ii) is reasonably available; and (iii) is willing" decides; (4): if not, a guardian on the same terms; (5): if not, "the person
-- responsible for the patient under section 110ZD".
-- INFERENCE: (2) is read with s 110S, so a treatment decision that does not operate (or is revoked) does not take priority.
-- s 119: for a matter "relating to their person other than -- (a) treatment ...; or (b) medical research", the enduring guardian (if
-- authorised, reasonably available and willing) decides; if not, the guardian on the same terms. s 119 names no-one further.
DECLARE Decider IS ONE OF
    `the person themselves`
    `the treatment decision in the directive`
    `the enduring guardian`
    `the guardian`
    `the person responsible`
    `no-one under the section`

GIVEN `able to make reasonable judgments about the treatment` IS A BOOLEAN, `a directive treatment decision covers the treatment and operates` IS A BOOLEAN, `an enduring guardian is authorised, available and willing` IS A BOOLEAN, `a guardian is authorised, available and willing` IS A BOOLEAN, `there is a person responsible under section 110ZD` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Decider
`who decides the treatment under section 110ZJ` MEANS
    IF `able to make reasonable judgments about the treatment` THEN `the person themselves`
    ELSE IF `a directive treatment decision covers the treatment and operates` THEN `the treatment decision in the directive`
        ELSE IF `an enduring guardian is authorised, available and willing` THEN `the enduring guardian`
            ELSE IF `a guardian is authorised, available and willing` THEN `the guardian`
                ELSE IF `there is a person responsible under section 110ZD` THEN `the person responsible`
                    ELSE `no-one under the section`

GIVEN `able to make reasonable judgments about the matter` IS A BOOLEAN, `an enduring guardian is authorised, available and willing` IS A BOOLEAN, `a guardian is authorised, available and willing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Decider
`who decides another personal matter under section 119` MEANS
    IF `able to make reasonable judgments about the matter` THEN `the person themselves`
    ELSE IF `an enduring guardian is authorised, available and willing` THEN `the enduring guardian`
        ELSE IF `a guardian is authorised, available and willing` THEN `the guardian`
            ELSE `no-one under the section`
